+//! Audio-frame-owned parked setup and whole-window participant tilt fitting.
+//! No Android dependencies or implicit system clock.
+//!
+//! Startup is Automatic at minimum volume, with the prepared player parked.
+//! An accepted first calibration reserves frame zero and waits for actual PCM
+//! playback, then consumes two complete cycles. Retries keep the same loop and
+//! reserve the next boundary. Actual pause during an attempt is terminal;
+//! previously fitted models retain source lineage through ordinary pauses.
+//!
+//! Ordinary bad samples mask quality rather than ending a window at frame zero.
+//! A causal 100 ms gravity estimate retains the 0.60/s motion threshold while
+//! separating high-rate noise. Original source vectors/timestamps are untouched.
+//! At 25 Hz, fit requires >=600/800 observations, >=280/cycle, >=60/phase and
+//! >=6 in both endpoint quarters of each ramp. Labels train the participant
+//! axis/direction/range; they are not a waveform-compliance test. Usable timed
+//! coverage and a nondegenerate mapping decide admission, not cue resemblance.
+//!
+//! Thirty-two healthy audio observations retain 250 ms history plus its bracket;
+//! up to 64 future training labels wait for a real audio observation. No frames
+//! are extrapolated. Actual-sample freshness/sensor gaps stay 200 ms, sensor/host
+//! drift stays 150 ms, and delivery/tail admission is separately bounded at250 ms.
+//! Hard source/audio generations still invalidate lineage. See the shared setup
+//! source contract for clock provenance and engineering qualification limits.
+//!
+//! Standalone host check (PowerShell; `-A dead_code` omits consumer-only APIs):
+//! `rustc --edition 2021 -A dead_code --test experiment_breathing_setup.rs -o
+//! $env:TEMP/experiment-breathing-setup-tests.exe`, then run that executable.
+
+use std::collections::VecDeque;
+
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
