+# Optional in-app Meta Platform update transport
+
+The selected composition now also requires `meta_required_version_manifest_url`
+equal to `https://viscereality.org/atmungsraum/quest-release.json`. Native owns
+fresh credential-free GETs, a 12-second caller deadline, 32KiB UTF-8 body limit,
+no redirect/304/cache fallback, strict duplicate-free object parsing and exact
+package/integer validation. Its minimum is a required floor; its latest remains
+a hint. SDK-observed newer availability also raises the persisted floor.
+Lower/stale responses and unavailable policy/Meta never lower that record.
+An unavailable check permits the loaded installed version with a warning only
+when no remembered higher floor exists and native releases a cycle grant.
+
+`NativeRendererMetaUpdateService` owns one automatic attempt per actual native
+cycle, plus explicit enrolled-controller attempts through the existing native
+main-looper journal. Manual body is exactly v/id/op/cycle/revision with
+`op=check-and-update`; receipt lookup v/id/op with `op=receipt` is read-only.
+The gateway serializes/binds mutating calls before dispatch. Replies retain
+original canonical body identity and the original accepted cycle/revision/nonce.
+No phone supplies SDK methods, version floors, URLs or package identity.
+Status v2 adds authoritative cycle/revision, retained last attempt, required
+floor, can_check and busy_reason. Status reads never start work.
+
+Matched SDK failures optionally add a closed `sdk_error` object:
+`{v:1,stage:1..6,code:<nonzero signed32>,http:null|100..599,install_result:<enum>}`.
+Its enum is exactly UNKNOWN, LOW_STORAGE, NETWORK_ERROR, DUPLICATE_REQUEST,
+INSTALLER_ERROR, USER_CANCELLED, AUTHORIZATION_ERROR or SUCCESS. The original
+SDK code is retained; adapter failures remain -1001 (missing/invalid error),
+-1002 (missing payload) and -1003 (unexpected SDK message type). HTTP outside
+100..599 becomes null. Only matched current-attempt replies update this record;
+the next admitted attempt clears it. Numeric/enum log diagnostics contain no
+App ID, request identity, raw exception or technical error text. Native parses
+at most256 bytes of technical error text for an exact, unambiguous enum token,
+then discards that text. Unknown, ambiguous and truncated text becomes UNKNOWN.
+Even an error containing SUCCESS remains an error, never install authority.
+
+A vendor DOWNLOAD error normalized to DUPLICATE_REQUEST permits one bounded
+fixed-current-app recovery per logical attempt. First a newly issued progress
+request must confirm a valid non-install app state (Entitled, DownloadQueued,
+Downloading or Installed), valid counters, the same actual loaded package,
+owner and native cycle. Installing/InstallQueued or an actual package change
+instead latch existing external-install uncertainty; they never cancel.
+Unknown/uninstall states, invalid counters and stale replies cannot cancel.
+This check does not identify or adopt the existing installer's target version.
+
+With monitor3 helper selected, the preferred recovery instead persists a pending target
+bound to the known higher channel offer and remembered floor, takes irreversible
+native admission, and requires positive helper ARM plus the existing main-looper
+kiosk latch. It then closes only its own idle app: stop its kiosk service, finish
+its own activities/task and terminate its own process. Main execution repeats
+owner/cycle/actual-PM checks and a five-second monotonic deadline; timed-out
+queued actions are expired and cannot later close the app. The final PM lookup
+is followed by another deadline check before any exit effect. Ordinary
+intentionalExit/cancel-watch is deliberately not used: the helper watch remains
+armed. Persistence/ARM/latch/exit failure never proceeds with a cooperative exit
+and retains the applicable pending/irreversible block. The reason is
+`queued-meta-update-handoff`, with installing/blocked status, not SDK-install proof.
+
+This selected lane issues neither SDK Cancel nor SDK Install. It does not
+assert which version the existing job contains. Only actual package replacement
+at/above the target and same-signer helper resolution permits replacement launch;
+the fresh process still verifies its pending target and policy. The helper's
+monitor3 capability continuously observes actual replacement and trusted
+launch-ready or explicit cancellation. It has no fixed download/installation
+expiry or fixed Meta launch grace. The five-second main command deadline above
+only expires stale callbacks; it never limits download monitoring.
+
+Without helper selected, recovery issues `CancelAppDownload` for the current app only. A matched
+positive cancel reply must have no SDK error and AppInstallResult Success7.
+Only then is a fresh GetVersion issued. It must retain actual installed/owner
+identity and a channel offer satisfying the remembered required floor before
+one new owned StartAppDownload is allowed. Neither cancellation nor progress
+proves a downloaded update. Positive owned Download Success7 and a progress
+request issued after that success remain mandatory before the unchanged
+durable pending/native admission/helper/kiosk/install sequence. A second
+duplicate is terminal. Probe/cancel/version stages each have15-second deadlines;
+owned downloads retain their10-minute/45-second total/stall checks. There is no
+retry loop, Meta database/global queue clearing, uninstall or permission change.
+
+Recovery exposes checking reasons `checking-duplicate-download` and
+`restarting-duplicate-download`. Unconfirmed cancellation, invalid state,
+repeated duplicates, changed owner/floor or timeout remain blocked with explicit
+reasons. This implements the documented request/response contracts; actual
+device queued-exit/cancellation and later install/relaunch require separate
+qualification. See the [official native API contract](https://developers.meta.com/vr/documentation/native/ps-in-app-update-apis/).
+
+Native `nativeCycleState()` supplies the cycle snapshot and
+`nativeFence(op,attempt,cycle,revision)` is the frozen compare-and-set seam:
+0 select, 1 begin, 2 ready, 3 valid, 4 irreversible install, 5 release grant,
+6 release blocked and 7 tighten external-install uncertainty. Begin/release
+advance revision; actual terminal writer completion plus parked audio advances
+the cycle. Actual safe owner retirement also invalidates its old grant/cycle.
+Java never resets native session_seen or fabricates a new preparation cycle.
+
+The SDK instance and initialization belong to the process. Attempts receive
+fresh logical IDs, a nonce-bound native predispatch admission and scoped retire.
+An old attempt is rejected before a C API call; retired responses cannot enter
+another attempt. Pending initialization alone survives retirement as process
+state. Cached success supports fresh GetVersion/download checks without
+reinitialization. Cached initialization failure is conservatively retained:
+`meta-platform-process-init-failed-restart-required` distinguishes it from
+retryable version/download/progress errors. A fresh process is needed for that
+SDK failure; a pending initialization may still finish on a subsequent check.
+No acquired/closed flag is reopened. Policy duration is excluded from the SDK's
+independent 15-second initialization/version deadline.
+
+Optional `experiment_meta_update_helper_enabled` selects only the fixed
+same-current-signer monitor3 helper and signature permission
+`org.viscereality.atmungsraum.boot.permission.UPDATE_HANDOFF` plus main
+`org.viscereality.atmungsraum.boot_protocol=3`. Both permission allowlist and
+declared manifest must include that exact permission.
+Selected helper adds only an exact `<queries><package>` visibility declaration
+for `org.viscereality.atmungsraum.boot`, required by its package/provider lookups;
+it is absent when helper is not selected. No broad package visibility permission
+is selected. Main validates helper
+package/provider ownership, protocol and exact current certificate set before
+ContentResolver calls. Selected own installation needs positive durable
+arm-update/watch ACK before SDK install dispatch. Trusted early launch sends
+started; a separate focused submitted-frame callback queues ready on the worker.
+ACKs use immutable loaded-process code and revalidate actual package identity.
+Explicit operator exit cancels the watch. Startup ready ACKs retry at most eight
+times while the same trusted owner remains current. Helper never installs.
+
+Before accepting helper ARM, the client additionally requires helper metadata
+`org.viscereality.atmungsraum.monitor_protocol=3`. Helper boot_protocol may remain2
+for immutable legacy-main compatibility, or be3; it is never sufficient alone.
+All new v1 calls add typed Integer monitor_protocol3 and Long boot_count plus
+deadline_elapsed (actual boot and elapsed time+5000ms). Arm has7 fields, ACK/cancel
+has5. Replies must explicitly report protocol3, monitor_protocol3, monitor=true
+and accepted=true; ARM additionally requires watching=true. Capability does not
+prove an active watch. Late/cross-boot replies cannot authorize an exit. Legacy
+helper2 without this capability returns
+`meta-update-helper-monitor-capability-required` and stays blocked without exit.
+Per-command unavailable/expired failures remain distinct. Neither command
+deadline nor finite focused-ready ACK retries impose a helper download timeout.
+
+Focused service controls:
+`python tools/checks/test_meta_update_startup.py`,
+`python tools/checks/test_meta_update_reusable_sdk.py`,
+`python tools/checks/test_meta_update_duplicate_recovery.py`,
+`python tools/checks/test_meta_update_queued_exit.py`,
+`python tools/checks/test_meta_update_queued_dispatch.py`,
+`python tools/checks/test_meta_update_service.py --json-jar <host-org-json-jar>`,
+`python tools/checks/test_meta_update_policy.py`, and
+`python tools/checks/test_meta_update_helper_client.py`.
+The monitor handshake is exercised by
+`python tools/checks/test_meta_update_helper_monitor.py`.
+The source/SDK closure binds all six service/client Java sources, the self-kiosk
+queued-exit owner, optional transport and three owned C++ files. Selected-helper
+actual DEX checks require both kiosk handoff and queued-exit method signatures.
+Actual package, delivery and
+hardware acceptance remain separate gates.
+
+`pwsh -NoProfile -File tools/checks/Test-MetaUpdateSourceClosure.ps1` executes
+the actual resolver inventory block against the packaging inventory and actual
+strict builder comparison before the SDK fixture compiles. Missing/tampered
+owners, unselected source records and disabled-path records are rejected.
+
+The native renderer's `experiment_meta_update_enabled` composition is disabled
+by default. Selection requires a canonical positive decimal `meta_platform_app_id`
+and the original native panel with the experiment command gateway. These are
+application inputs; this repository provides no production App ID.
+
+The build also requires `-EnableMetaPlatformUpdate`, `-MetaPlatformSdkRoot`,
+`-MetaPlatformHeadersSha256`, `-MetaPlatformLoaderSha256` and
+`-MetaPlatformArchiveSha256`. No ambient SDK lookup selects this route.
+SDK207 is externally supplied under the [Oculus SDK License Agreement](https://developer.oculus.com/licenses/oculussdk/).
+The user/build owner must accept that license before supplying the SDK.
+No Meta SDK header, library, archive, Java SDK or Kotlin runtime is redistributed
+as repository source. Official archive provenance SHA256 is
+`00c4035dce5cda094eaf0272ad70f2deda389c32bf0d3eacc12135c16d385401`.
+This provenance value records the accepted supplier; the separately explicit
+header and loader digests bind the actual compiler/packaging bytes.
+
+`tools/lib/meta_platform_packaging.py headers --sdk-root <explicit-root>` emits
+the header inventory hash. It hashes UTF-8 JSON with ordinal path order,
+sorted object keys, compact separators, ASCII escapes and no newline. Each
+Include-relative file record contains `path`, `sha256` and `bytes`. Every
+selected header is bounded and included; links and non-header files fail.
+SDK version macros must be 1.207.0.0. The loader must be ELF64 AArch64 with
+SONAME `libovrplatformloader.so`, only libc/libdl/liblog dependencies, and
+16KiB-aligned PT_LOAD segments. Both headers and loader are checked again
+before compilation/staging. Owned source hashes, external digests, provenance
+and this notice enter the selection fingerprint and ignored build evidence.
+
+`NativeRendererMetaPlatformTransport` owns the SDK's single process message
+queue and is selected only with this composition. A single coordinator worker
+serializes asynchronous initialize/version/download/progress/install/cancel
+requests and nonblocking polls. Every popped message is freed, including stale
+IDs. Pending IDs and actual message types must agree; null payloads and SDK
+errors remain explicit failures. Progress status and install-result enums are
+distinct. Errors expose only bounded numeric/whitelisted enum diagnostics, not
+raw technical messages or installation authority.
+Install always passes null default relaunch options. Closing prevents future
+requests and delivery; a new transport cannot acquire the SDK in that process.
+No SDK call or message pump occurs on the XR render thread.
+
+The JNI wrapper is freshly compiled against selected SDK207 headers and loader
+using NDK27.2, static libc++ and 16KiB linker page sizes. Java uses the selected
+Java17 toolchain with Java8-compatible output. The final signed APK check joins
+actual all-DEX class/method definitions, exact owned JNI/SDK-loader hashes and
+their arm64 entries. SDK-off builds reject either transport definitions or
+native libraries. The source manifest's App ID/update metadata is checked
+before build, and the actual final manifest dump is checked after packaging.
+No permission, install authority or lifecycle trust comes from this transport.
+
+Focused host checks: `python tools/checks/test_meta_platform_packaging.py` and
+`pwsh -NoProfile -File tools/checks/Test-MetaPlatformTransport.ps1 -SdkRoot <explicit-root>`.
+These compile production transport code with actual SDK207 headers and fake
+SDK leaves; they establish request/error/type/lifetime behavior, not headset
+delivery, entitlement, installation or relaunch acceptance. That requires a
+Meta-managed increasing-version transition and observed new package identity.
