+# Immutable particle visual profile
+
+An app-owned private particle payload can select `particle-visual-profile`
+without selecting the Showcase product, menus, acquisition runtime or input
+sources. The locked APK builder selects it only for the explicit payload input
+`RUSTY_QUEST_NATIVE_RENDERER_PRIVATE_PARTICLE_VISUAL_PROFILE=true`, a selected
+`renderer.private_particles`, the V1 frame extension, and a SHA-256 digest in
+`RUSTY_QUEST_NATIVE_RENDERER_PRIVATE_PARTICLE_VISUAL_PROFILE_SHA256`.
+
+The private data directory must contain `particle-visual-profile.json`. The
+build embeds its exact bytes; the render adapter checks their digest and uses
+the existing particle-dynamics parser. Invalid data prevents particle drawing.
+The generic driver bank reserves the same two extension rows as Showcase;
+the private shader owns their downstream interpretation.
+
+Defaults apply when the renderer first draws and are restored by an explicit
+product reset, including a reset pending before the first draw. They do not
+reset oscillator phases, replace the experiment breath driver, write a new
+progress value, or recenter the world anchor. The current accepted driver-zero
+progress supplies both the configured radius interpolation and the frame
+extension. Explicit material coefficients retain the same precedence as the
+Showcase render path.
+
+This feature does not start sensors, alter calibration or session timing,
+grant a command capability, or enable any UI. Product input selection and
+session policy stay with their existing owners. Default and Showcase builds
+retain their original feature selections. Private tuning and payload contents
+must remain downstream-owned.
+
+Host verification uses `cargo test -p rusty-quest-native-renderer-android-native
+--lib --features particle-visual-profile -- --test-threads=1`; the existing
+setup tests share a process-wide selection override and require serialization.
+Set the private data directory and profile digest inputs above to exercise the
+actual packaged profile; without those inputs the host build uses an inert
+placeholder and the packaged-profile test does not claim payload validation.
+`python tools/checks/test_particle_visual_profile_reset.py .` runs the actual
+renderer reset method with inert platform adapters, checking repeated resets
+and a reset pending before first draw. Android qualification must also compile
+the actual selected renderer/shader closure. Neither host tests nor compilation
+establish device rendering parity.
