 # Polar connection and stream recovery
 
+The selected native experiment breathing composition requests both ACC and ECG
+from its current connected Polar sensor without a phone Start-PMD action. This
+requires strict selected metadata, the actual live native product host and accepted
+native feature-lock/activation readback. Other/manual compositions retain their
+selected-stream defaults. Explicit individual/all stream Stops remain authoritative,
+including before connection and across exact-sensor recovery.
+
+A main-handler recovery monitor serializes the existing probe/settings/START flow
+until its sensor result or actual current-connection data is known. Write completion
+and START acknowledgement alone do not establish sample readiness. Definite
+no-effect/rejected attempts retry after two seconds, capped at ten seconds after
+repeated failures. A missing write/START/data outcome is observed for up to fifteen
+seconds, then retires that GATT and uses the existing exact-sensor connection
+recovery; it never blindly resends an uncertain START. Fresh data suspends effects;
+the low-rate monitor can detect later signal loss. Owner/feature retirement,
+connection replacement and explicit desired Stops fence queued work. This never
+resumes a paused main experiment or opens a permission/settings prompt.
+Matched STOP acknowledgements and explicit new START intents advance separate
+stream receipt floors. Cached earlier data cannot restore a stopped stream or
+certify the new request as receiving samples.
+
+The optional compact `y.ar` Boolean describes active selected acquisition demand
+for both streams on the exact connected/subscribed GATT. An explicit Stop of either
+stream makes it false; unselected legacy compositions omit it. Readiness remains
+the separate actual-data fields.
+
+Only authenticated, enrolled private-LAN status can add `y.ad`: one latest valid
+decoded ACC frame with `frame_type`, `active_rate_hz`, `frame_samples`, decimal-string
+`sensor_end_ns`, `frame_receipt_java_ns`, `receipt_delta_ns`, raw parsed `first_mg`
+and `last_mg` triples, and `max_adjacent_mg`. The latter is the largest absolute
+adjacent difference on any XYZ axis, capped at the signed 32-bit maximum. The owner
+stores one typed frame and creates JSON only on read. GATT/generation retirement
+clears it; guest/public BLE and relay status never contain it. The protocol strips
+the private diagnostic from non-LAN and nonprivate-LAN responses before signing.
+No packet codec, timestamp or
+recording equation changes accompany this diagnostic. Device format, simultaneous
+streams and physical recovery still require the next attended qualification.
+
+Focused controls: `test_polar_required_stream_recovery.py` executes current PMD
+entrypoints, queue callbacks and the semantic owner; `test_polar_required_stream_scope.py`
+executes native selection, intent projection and bounded private-frame readback.
+The selected gateway tests separately check authenticated export and guest exclusion.
+
+Selected native phone-control products use one attended startup permission
+coordinator for Polar and discovery. It requests the needed declared runtime
+closure after the real Activity resumes, independently of whether the app panel
+is visible or a trusted session cold-launch epoch was admitted. This permission
+request does not create sensor/session intent. A denied request is not retried in
+a resume loop; one cancelled request may retry on a later resume. Metadata-off
+products retain their existing permission behavior.
+
+Global Location services remain a separate scanning prerequisite. With declared
+Polar SCAN and granted runtime permissions, the selected host may present the
+ordinary Android Location-settings surface once; it never toggles Location.
+Returning rechecks actual state. The compact setup projection's optional `l`
+reports this state separately from app permission `p` and Bluetooth `b`; existing
+connected ACC/ECG streams remain represented independently.
+
